From e2af0f1a4029fda721e916c77579c152a1f059a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Max Buster <maxbuster@Maxs-Mac-mini.local>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 16:21:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] PR #269 test toggle: setStopRecordingOnMute switch on connect
 screen

Wires webrtc-sdk PR #269 (Android ADM stop-on-mute opt-out) through
LiveKitOverrides.AudioOptions.javaAudioDeviceModuleCustomizer:

- Switch on MainActivity connect screen (default OFF = exercise PR path)
- Persisted via MainViewModel PREFERENCES_KEY_STOP_ON_MUTE
- Plumbed via CallActivity.BundleArgs -> CallViewModel(stopRecordingOnMute)
- Applied to JavaAudioDeviceModule.Builder in AudioOptions customizer
- Logs 'PR269: setStopRecordingOnMute(<value>)' at LKLog.i for verification

Also (build changes required to consume a local custom WebRTC AAR):
- settings.gradle: add flatDir { dirs livekit-android-sdk/libs }
- livekit-android-sdk/build.gradle: api libs.webrtc -> api(name: 'libwebrtc', ext: 'aar')
- sample-app-common/build.gradle: disable LeakCanary
  (2.8.1 vs androidx.lifecycle < 2.9 causes AbstractMethodError on activity start)
---
 libs-note.txt                                 |  7 +++++
 livekit-android-sdk/build.gradle              |  2 +-
 sample-app-common/build.gradle                |  2 +-
 .../livekit/android/sample/CallViewModel.kt   | 11 +++++++
 .../livekit/android/sample/MainViewModel.kt   | 10 ++++++
 .../android/composesample/CallActivity.kt     |  2 ++
 .../android/composesample/MainActivity.kt     | 31 +++++++++++++++----
 settings.gradle                               |  1 +
 8 files changed, 58 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 libs-note.txt

diff --git a/libs-note.txt b/libs-note.txt
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..aa1e788
--- /dev/null
+++ b/libs-note.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+This branch expects libwebrtc.aar (~13MB) at:
+  livekit-android-sdk/libs/libwebrtc.aar
+
+That AAR is built from webrtc-sdk/webrtc PR #269 (branch: android-stop-on-mute-optout)
+with the android_prefixed pipeline (patches + Shadow relocate + rename to
+liblkjingle_peerconnection_so.so). Do NOT commit it to git; publish as a
+GitHub Release asset instead.
